  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the Eastern Partnership Regional Road Safety Observatory (EaP RSO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Supporting the Eastern Partnership Regional Road Safety Observatory (EaP RSO) - The action&#xbf;s overall objective is to support the Eastern Partner countries in improving land transport safety by providing the required support to promptly and efficiently advance towards the reduction of road traffic fatal and non-fatal injuries. For this purpose, the action will develop a solid body of evidence-based approaches in the area of road safety in the EaP region. The action will support the set-up and operation of a regional Eastern Partnership Road Safety Observatory (EaP RSO) in line with the 2018 Eastern Partnership Declaration on Road Safety that sets the target of reducing the number of fatal and serious road traffic injuries by 50% from 2020 to 2030. The EaP Road Safety Observatory aims to reinforce national road safety data collection, facilitate the creation of more robust national road safety systems and provide the necessary evidence for efficient policy making. The Observatory will also serve as a platform for sharing best practices and as a tool for benchmarking road safety performance. Consequently, the action will provide necessary assistance to improve the quality of the road safety-related data and knowledge on road safety performance, which is essential for the design of strategies and measures in order to achieve this reduction in road casualties.</narrative>
  </description>
